-- HAND-APPLIED ONLY (the *.sql.disabled suffix is load-bearing). Prod deploys do NOT run startup
-- migrations (main.startup() returns early in fast mode, SKIP_HEAVY_STARTUP_INIT='true'), so no deploy
-- applies this file; the suffix also keeps it out of the boot runner wherever the full startup runs.
--
-- RUNBOOK (out of band, one-off job, controller slot): BEFORE EXTERNAL_REFERRAL_REFRESH_CATALOGUE_ENABLED
-- is switched on, not before the merge. Nothing reads or writes the column until the lane runs, and a
-- lane run that does not find it stays off (`external_referral_readiness._page_read_column_ready`).
--   * ADD COLUMN without a default is a catalogue-only change, but it takes ACCESS EXCLUSIVE on the
--     table for that instant, and queued behind a long reader it would block every read behind it.
--     The file bounds that wait itself (SET LOCAL lock_timeout below), so run its statements in ONE
--     transaction (db.sql_migrations.split_statements, as 260's job does; on autocommit SET LOCAL is a
--     no-op), outside the refresh, sweep and drain runs, and retry the whole file on a lock timeout.
--   * No backfill. A NULL column falls back to last_crawled_at, which every refresh before the lane
--     set from a page read; the lane's first catalogue read of a seed copies that value in.
--
-- 274: when the seed refresh last read the seed's PAGE (`services.external_seed_catalogue_refresh`).
-- The catalogue price lane re-prices a seed from its store's /products.json and moves last_crawled_at
-- without reading the page, so the page read it defers to every page_max_age_days() needs a stamp of
-- its own. It cannot live in seed_data: the retailer-ingest drain's upsert replaces seed_data whole
-- (`apply._SEED_UPSERT_SQL`) on its ~120 h re-enqueue, and never names this column.
--   * a page read of the served product in a lane run sets it to NOW();
--   * a catalogue read sets it to COALESCE(last_page_read_at, last_crawled_at), read from the row as it
--     was before the statement's own last_crawled_at = NOW().
-- schema-guard-exempt: read and written only by a catalogue-lane run that has checked the column exists (flag default off); kept off the self-heal so no boot path races ACCESS EXCLUSIVE.

SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '3s';

ALTER TABLE external_product_seeds ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS last_page_read_at TIMESTAMPTZ;

COMMENT ON COLUMN external_product_seeds.last_page_read_at IS
  'When the seed refresh last read this seed''s page (the catalogue lane carries it across its own reads). NULL = no catalogue read yet: last_crawled_at is the page read.';
